244
00:25:34.955 --> 00:25:37.207
Get rid of that gum.

245
00:25:37.249 --> 00:25:40.168
- You got a tissue?
- And your hotel bill.

246
00:25:40.252 --> 00:25:43.129
- Thanks.
- Don't lose those. Keep them in the envelope.

247
00:25:43.296 --> 00:25:45.131
We've got the new specs for the dam.

248
00:25:45.257 --> 00:25:47.592
- Great, Louie. I'll check those out.
- Here.

249
00:25:47.759 --> 00:25:51.513
- Is Eddie here?
- The door's unlocked.

250
00:25:51.596 --> 00:25:53.848
- Morning, pal.
- How you doing?

251
00:25:54.015 --> 00:25:56.601
Same old same old.
People need killing.

252
00:25:56.768 --> 00:25:58.270
Oh, Johnny.

253
00:25:58.395 --> 00:26:00.939
Little get-together this weekend at my house.

254
00:26:01.106 --> 00:26:04.609
Barbecue, no ladies, dudes only.
It's gonna be awesome.

255
00:26:04.734 --> 00:26:06.945
Yeah, I'll talk to the missus.

256
00:26:07.070 --> 00:26:09.614
You want to use my cellphone?
Maybe give her a call,

257
00:26:09.739 --> 00:26:12.868
in case you decide to scratch your ass
or use the head later.

258
00:26:12.993 --> 00:26:16.705
- Make sure she thinks it's OK.
- You live with your mother.

259
00:26:16.788 --> 00:26:19.583
Why bring her into this?
She's a first-class lady.

260
00:26:19.749 --> 00:26:24.254
And I don't have to check in with her when I
want to do something. She cooks, she cleans.

261
00:26:24.421 --> 00:26:27.215
She makes me snacks.
I'm the dumb guy?

262
00:26:43.315 --> 00:26:45.192
John Smith.

263
00:26:48.737 --> 00:26:51.865
- Hello, John.
- Morning, Atlanta.

264
00:26:51.990 --> 00:26:56.995
Quite the body count this week. We have
a priority one, so I need your expertise.

265
00:26:57.162 --> 00:27:01.708
The target's name is Benjamin Danz,
aka "The Tank".

266
00:27:02.209 --> 00:27:06.087
He's a direct threat to the firm.
DIA custody.

267
00:27:06.213 --> 00:27:11.509
They're making a ground-to-air handoff
to heli, ten miles north of the Mexican border.

268
00:27:11.593 --> 00:27:15.180
I need you to make sure
the target does not change hands.

269
00:27:15.347 --> 00:27:16.556
"The Tank"?

270
00:27:38.870 --> 00:27:41.581
- L-Temp technology...
- Jane Smith confirmed.

271
00:27:41.748 --> 00:27:43.959
Stand by for contact.

272
00:27:44.042 --> 00:27:46.336
Sorry to interrupt, but we have a situation.

273
00:27:46.461 --> 00:27:50.966
You know the competition would love to see
us burn. I need you to handle this personally.

274
00:27:51.049 --> 00:27:53.051
- Target?
- Benjamin Danz.

275
00:27:53.218 --> 00:27:57.514
I'm rolling the specs now.
We need this quick, clean, and contained.

276
00:27:57.639 --> 00:27:58.682
Yes, sir.

277
00:28:06.857 --> 00:28:08.608
- Ladies.
- Morning.

278
00:28:08.692 --> 00:28:10.360
- Morning.
- Hello, Jane.

279
00:28:12.320 --> 00:28:15.198
Yesterday's op: One kill,
one agent in protective custody.

280
00:28:15.365 --> 00:28:17.742
- We'll get him out tomorrow.
- Two cases of G-40s.

281
00:28:17.868 --> 00:28:20.036
- The grenade launchers are here.
- Order more.

282
00:28:20.203 --> 00:28:22.247
All right. Go, Jas.

283
00:28:22.414 --> 00:28:25.250
The target's name is Benjamin Danz,
aka "The Tank".

284
00:28:25.417 --> 00:28:27.210
- You serious?
- Yeah.

285
00:28:27.335 --> 00:28:30.046
He's being moved across the border
to a federal facility.

286
00:28:30.213 --> 00:28:33.967
The only point of vulnerability
is just south of the border.

287
00:28:34.050 --> 00:28:38.263
I want GPS and SAC of the canyon,
and the weather report for the last three days.

288
00:28:39.598 --> 00:28:45.312
He'll rendezvous with the helicopter at a
deserted airstrip. We've one chance to strike.

289
00:28:47.981 --> 00:28:50.150
Oh, look. More desert.

290
00:29:21.139 --> 00:29:24.809
- Are we green?
- Perimeter is armed. We are up and running.

291
00:29:37.864 --> 00:29:41.535
Red team, red team, this is Broadway Joe.
Half-time is approaching.

292
00:29:41.701 --> 00:29:43.912
Copy that, Broadway Joe.

293
00:30:17.988 --> 00:30:20.198
Oh, come on...

294
00:30:28.081 --> 00:30:32.085
- You getting this?
- Affirmative. Is it a threat?

295
00:30:34.713 --> 00:30:37.716
Countdown's initiated.
The convoy is not in the zone yet.

296
00:30:37.799 --> 00:30:40.302
An idiot's in the field.
He'll blow the charges.

297
00:31:02.782 --> 00:31:04.743
OK.

298
00:31:12.250 --> 00:31:14.461
You gotta be kidding me.

299
00:31:17.631 --> 00:31:19.382
Civilians.

300
00:31:31.603 --> 00:31:33.980
Let's get a tune out of this trombone.

301
00:31:38.568 --> 00:31:40.487
Picking up a weapon signature.

302
00:31:40.612 --> 00:31:42.739
Shit. Not a civilian.

303
00:31:45.617 --> 00:31:47.661
Aw, man...

304
00:31:47.786 --> 00:31:48.703
Asshole.

305
00:31:58.588 --> 00:32:00.549
Countdown is initiated.

306
00:32:23.280 --> 00:32:25.657
You should so not be allowed
to buy these things.

307
00:32:34.082 --> 00:32:35.250
Abort!

308
00:33:15.248 --> 00:33:18.168
I think I got ID'd on that hit.
You ever been ID'd on a hit?

309
00:33:18.293 --> 00:33:21.296
- Not that I'm aware of, no.
- Right. I'm in trouble.

310
00:33:21.379 --> 00:33:26.051
- You get a look at him?
- Little thing. Buck ten, buck fifteen tops.

311
00:33:26.218 --> 00:33:28.720
Maybe he's Filipino.

312
00:33:28.803 --> 00:33:31.014
I'm not even sure it was a him.

313
00:33:32.641 --> 00:33:35.560
You saying that you had
your ass handed to you by some girl?

314
00:33:35.685 --> 00:33:38.104
I think so. A pro.

315
00:33:39.856 --> 00:33:44.152
Well, it shouldn't be that difficult. I mean,
how many chicks are hitters out there?

316
00:33:44.194 --> 00:33:46.988
- You guys want any dessert?
- What do you have, honey?

317
00:33:47.155 --> 00:33:50.158
- Ice cream.
- Delicious. What flavors?

318
00:33:50.242 --> 00:33:52.786
- Chocolate and vanilla.
- I don't like those.

319
00:33:52.953 --> 00:33:56.414
But mixed together,
that could be nice, you know what I mean?

320
00:33:56.498 --> 00:34:00.043
And not just the little pink spoon,
I like the whole sundae.

321
00:34:00.210 --> 00:34:02.087
- That could be arranged.
- Perfect.

322
00:34:02.212 --> 00:34:06.800
"Could be arranged. " You hear that? I'd like
to have her kick my ass, know what I mean?

323
00:34:06.967 --> 00:34:10.470
- Any other details besides her weight class?
- Laptop.

324
00:34:10.595 --> 00:34:12.597
Sorry? You're in a whole zone right now...

325
00:34:12.764 --> 00:34:14.432
- Laptop.
- OK, laptop.

326
00:34:14.891 --> 00:34:17.561
I want to know who that bitch is.
Get me that tape.

327
00:34:17.644 --> 00:34:20.188
- Jane.
- Get me that tape.

328
00:34:20.355 --> 00:34:22.566
- What?
- It's Father.

329
00:34:29.114 --> 00:34:32.242
The FBI secured the package.
The window's closed, sir.

330
00:34:32.409 --> 00:34:35.745
- I told you we couldn't afford mistakes.
- There was another player.

331
00:34:35.912 --> 00:34:42.294
We do not leave witnesses.
If this player ID'd you... You know the rules.

332
00:34:42.419 --> 00:34:45.213
You have 48 hours to clean the scene, Jane.

333
00:34:45.338 --> 00:34:47.549
Looking forward to it, sir.

334
00:34:50.385 --> 00:34:54.139
All right, we have a new target.
Let's find out who he is.

335
00:34:56.182 --> 00:34:59.519
Jesus... What did you do to it?

336
00:34:59.936 --> 00:35:02.397
Put a campfire out with it?

337
00:35:02.564 --> 00:35:04.608
Buy a new one.

338
00:35:04.816 --> 00:35:07.986
This one has sentimental value for its owner.

339
00:35:08.153 --> 00:35:12.365
- Who's that?
- Well, Gwen, I'm just hoping you can tell me.

340
00:35:13.909 --> 00:35:17.287
So, why you gotta know so bad, anyway?

341
00:35:18.288 --> 00:35:20.916
You know, just trying
to return some lost property.

342
00:35:20.999 --> 00:35:23.752
- Hey, Phil.
- Hey, John.

343
00:35:24.753 --> 00:35:27.088
- You a vegan?
- No.

344
00:35:27.214 --> 00:35:29.257
My girlfriend is.

345
00:35:30.884 --> 00:35:33.136
Here we go.

346
00:35:33.303 --> 00:35:36.181
Upgraded RAM module.

347
00:35:39.267 --> 00:35:41.269
Chip's Chinese.

348
00:35:41.436 --> 00:35:45.982
Imported by Dynamix. Retailed by...

349
00:35:47.692 --> 00:35:52.239
You know, I might be able
to get you a billing address.

350
00:35:52.364 --> 00:35:54.991
All right? No name, just an address.

351
00:35:55.158 --> 00:35:59.412
570 Lexington Avenue, Suite 5003.

352
00:35:59.538 --> 00:36:01.498
New York.

353
00:36:01.581 --> 00:36:03.792
You know the place?

354
00:36:38.201 --> 00:36:40.495
Sweet Jesus! Mother of God...

355
00:36:58.013 --> 00:37:00.932
Why don't you both go make some coffee?

356
00:37:20.785 --> 00:37:23.330
Jane, it's your husband.

357
00:37:24.539 --> 00:37:29.294
He's back from Atlanta
and he wants to know about dinner.

358
00:37:29.419 --> 00:37:32.297
Tell him... Dinner's at seven.

359
00:37:32.797 --> 00:37:36.551
Hi, John.
Yeah, she says dinner's at seven.

360
00:37:36.635 --> 00:37:38.845
It always is.

361
00:38:45.996 --> 00:38:47.998
Perfect timing.

362
00:38:48.206 --> 00:38:50.792
As always.

363
00:38:54.838 --> 00:38:57.632
- This is a nice surprise.
- I hope so.

364
00:38:57.799 --> 00:39:00.635
- You're home early.
- I missed you.

365
00:39:01.720 --> 00:39:04.014
I missed you, too.

366
00:39:04.097 --> 00:39:06.516
- Shall we?
- Yes.

367
00:39:19.779 --> 00:39:24.743
- Thought these were for special occasions.
- This is a special occasion.

368
00:39:54.397 --> 00:39:57.067
Pot roast. My favorite.

369
00:40:00.987 --> 00:40:03.406
Allow me, sweetheart.

370
00:40:03.532 --> 00:40:05.700
Been on your feet all day.

371
00:40:05.784 --> 00:40:07.786
Thank you.

372
00:40:07.953 --> 00:40:10.163
Sure.

373
00:40:24.302 --> 00:40:27.013
So how's work?

374
00:40:29.099 --> 00:40:32.561
Actually, we had a little trouble
with a commission.

375
00:40:32.644 --> 00:40:34.563
- Is that right?
- Yeah.

376
00:40:35.647 --> 00:40:38.942
Double booking with another firm.

377
00:40:39.067 --> 00:40:41.570
- Green beans?
- No, thank you.

378
00:40:41.736 --> 00:40:43.905
You'll have some.

379
00:40:47.742 --> 00:40:49.786
Well, I hope everything worked out OK.

380
00:40:49.911 --> 00:40:51.788
It hasn't yet.

381
00:40:51.955 --> 00:40:54.666
But it will.

382
00:41:01.798 --> 00:41:04.092
Pot roast is my favorite.

383
00:41:04.217 --> 00:41:06.970
Sweetheart, could you pass the salt?

384
00:41:42.339 --> 00:41:44.591
Tried something new?

385
00:42:00.982 --> 00:42:02.984
How was Atlanta?

386
00:42:03.985 --> 00:42:08.490
Had a few problems ourselves.
Some figures didn't add up.

387
00:42:08.615 --> 00:42:11.243
- Big deal?
- Life or death. Wine?

388
00:42:34.516 --> 00:42:36.560
- I got it.
- I'll get a towel.

389
00:42:48.196 --> 00:42:50.115
Janie?

390
00:42:53.535 --> 00:42:55.495
Honey?

391
00:43:03.211 --> 00:43:05.005
Jane!

392
00:43:11.344 --> 00:43:12.929
Jane!

393
00:43:16.099 --> 00:43:18.018
How could I be so stupid?

394
00:43:28.695 --> 00:43:29.988
Jane!

395
00:43:30.197 --> 00:43:31.990
Jane!

396
00:43:50.550 --> 00:43:52.886
Oh, dear God...

397
00:44:00.310 --> 00:44:02.771
Wait. No, no. Accident.

398
00:44:02.854 --> 00:44:04.981
Honey? Accident.

399
00:44:05.106 --> 00:44:07.734
Jane, stop the car, now.

400
00:44:08.652 --> 00:44:10.737
Jane?

401
00:44:10.862 --> 00:44:12.739
You're overreacting.

402
00:44:13.949 --> 00:44:15.909
Let's not get carried away.

403
00:44:15.992 --> 00:44:18.620
We don't want to go to sleep angry.
We can talk this out.

404
00:44:18.745 --> 00:44:19.829
God!

405
00:44:19.996 --> 00:44:21.581
Pull over.

406
00:44:21.748 --> 00:44:24.209
Pull over! Pull over!

407
00:44:26.419 --> 00:44:28.213
Now, look...

408
00:44:33.009 --> 00:44:35.220
We need to talk!

409
00:44:45.355 --> 00:44:49.317
- OK, I'm coming. Who is it?
- Open up.

410
00:44:51.611 --> 00:44:54.489
- What the hell happened to you?
- My wife.

411
00:45:00.453 --> 00:45:02.914
- She tried to kill me.
- Yes. And you know what?

412
00:45:03.039 --> 00:45:07.210
Gladys tried to kill me. Not with a car.
At least Jane was a man about it.

413
00:45:07.335 --> 00:45:12.549
But they all try to kill you. Slowly, painfully,
cripplingly. And then, wham! They hurt you.

414
00:45:12.632 --> 00:45:16.011
You know how hurt I used to be?
I used to beat myself up. Now I'm great.

415
00:45:16.136 --> 00:45:19.347
I got dates all the time.
I just woke up from a thing, I'm in my robe.

416
00:45:19.431 --> 00:45:21.391
- You live with your mom.
- I choose to.

417
00:45:21.558 --> 00:45:25.270
Because that's the only woman
I've ever trusted.

418
00:45:27.397 --> 00:45:30.692
- It's unbelievable.
- Look, I know exactly what you're thinking.

419
00:45:30.817 --> 00:45:33.695
If she lied about that,
what else has she lied about?

420
00:45:33.820 --> 00:45:36.865
I mean, her job is a spy,
to get information from people.

421
00:45:36.990 --> 00:45:41.661
French Riviera. A yacht. An Iranian prince.

422
00:45:41.786 --> 00:45:46.082
She's supposed to get close to him
and gain his trust. It's disgusting.

423
00:45:46.208 --> 00:45:48.210
What? What are you saying?

424
00:45:48.293 --> 00:45:52.047
What? Your husband is the shooter?

425
00:45:52.214 --> 00:45:54.382
That's impossible.

426
00:45:55.759 --> 00:45:56.760
Really?

427
00:45:56.885 --> 00:46:00.805
This was probably planned from
the beginning. Operation Stakeout Johnny.

428
00:46:00.889 --> 00:46:05.519
A six-year stakeout to get information
from you. Mission accomplished.

429
00:46:07.979 --> 00:46:09.356
OK.

430
00:46:10.357 --> 00:46:12.442
Here's the upside.

431
00:46:12.609 --> 00:46:14.444
- You don't love him.
- No.

432
00:46:14.611 --> 00:46:18.782
You'll kill him, and nobody's
better at that than you are.

433
00:46:18.949 --> 00:46:22.202
- Thank you.
- And then it'll be over.

434
00:46:28.083 --> 00:46:31.753
Lookit, I know you're embarrassed,
but it's Eddie you're talking to.

435
00:46:31.836 --> 00:46:35.006
The guys we work with,
they don't know, I'm never gonna tell 'em.

436
00:46:35.131 --> 00:46:39.761
The people she works with probably got
a big laugh over this, but that's not important.

437
00:46:39.886 --> 00:46:43.431
Lookit, it's like 150 pages
of a book have been written.

438
00:46:43.598 --> 00:46:47.143
In the first 150 pages, Johnny's been a clown.

439
00:46:47.269 --> 00:46:53.692
Well, you can write the last ten pages. You
been smoked, but you can write the last ten.

440
00:46:53.817 --> 00:46:57.571
Great talk, man. We should do it more often.
It was great, I'm proud of you.

441
00:46:57.696 --> 00:47:00.699
- I'm gonna borrow this.
- I like where your head's at, man.

442
00:47:00.782 --> 00:47:02.701
- I'll do it in the morning.
- Yeah.

443
00:47:04.202 --> 00:47:05.453
- You OK?
- Yeah.

444
00:47:05.620 --> 00:47:08.164
- OK. Good night.
- Night.

445
00:47:22.929 --> 00:47:24.764
You don't love him.

446
00:47:24.890 --> 00:47:27.684
- Night, Johnny.
- Night, Eddie.

447
00:47:27.809 --> 00:47:30.020
Good night, Mom.

448
00:48:16.066 --> 00:48:17.609
OK, girls. Let's go.

449
00:48:17.734 --> 00:48:21.238
Pocket litter, receipts, matchbooks.
You know the drill.

450
00:48:39.589 --> 00:48:42.759
This is nice. Who picked this out?

451
00:48:45.303 --> 00:48:47.764
- What is this?
- It looks like your wedding.

452
00:48:47.889 --> 00:48:51.268
- I know what it is. What are you doing?
- Research on the target.

453
00:48:51.351 --> 00:48:53.562
This room is wrapped. Thank you.

454
00:48:54.646 --> 00:49:00.610
...to have and to hold,
to love and to cherish, till death do us part.

455
00:49:00.694 --> 00:49:03.154
I promise.

456
00:49:03.238 --> 00:49:08.243
I, John, take you, Jane, to be my lawfully
wedded wife, to have and to h...

457
00:49:15.709 --> 00:49:17.919
What's going on, Mrs. Smith?

458
00:49:18.837 --> 00:49:20.213
Garden party, girls.

459
00:49:28.847 --> 00:49:31.600
Howdy, neighbor.

460
00:49:37.731 --> 00:49:42.068
Wow. I can't believe I've never
been in here before. This is great.

461
00:49:42.194 --> 00:49:45.405
- Start with the living room.
- Oh, yeah.

462
00:49:45.530 --> 00:49:50.452
- I love the floors. What are they, teak?
- Red oak, Martin. Red oak.

463
00:49:51.411 --> 00:49:55.999
And you won the Golf Masters trophy
this year.

464
00:49:56.166 --> 00:49:59.461
- Again.
- Again. That'll be on your mantel next year.

465
00:50:29.699 --> 00:50:30.909
Bitch.

466
00:50:35.705 --> 00:50:38.166
Target profile is our main priority.

467
00:50:39.167 --> 00:50:41.044
Utilize all means necessary.

468
00:50:41.211 --> 00:50:45.090
Phone taps. Credit cards.
Audio scan civilian frequencies.

469
00:50:45.215 --> 00:50:47.384
With what, Jane?

470
00:50:49.511 --> 00:50:52.514
You've reached the Smiths.
We can't take your call,

471
00:50:52.597 --> 00:50:55.851
but leave a message after the tone
and we'll get back to you.

472
00:50:56.017 --> 00:51:00.063
- And search the database.
- For what? John Smith?

473
00:51:02.816 --> 00:51:06.194
- Find him.
- Jane?

474
00:51:06.361 --> 00:51:07.821
What?

475
00:51:07.904 --> 00:51:10.407
- I think I found him.
- Where?

476
00:51:10.448 --> 00:51:12.659
Here.

477
00:51:14.619 --> 00:51:17.080
Heat sensor breach in the perimeter.

478
00:51:17.205 --> 00:51:20.500
Commence scanning all floors.

479
00:51:23.253 --> 00:51:25.755
I told you not to bother me
at the office, honey.

480
00:51:25.839 --> 00:51:31.469
- Well, you are still Mrs. Smith.
- Well, so are a lot of girls.

481
00:51:31.595 --> 00:51:34.097
Careful. I can push the button
any time, anywhere.

482
00:51:34.181 --> 00:51:37.559
Baby, you couldn't find the button
with both hands and a map.

483
00:51:39.686 --> 00:51:42.480
Last warning. You need to disappear.

484
00:51:42.606 --> 00:51:43.732
- No.
- Now.

485
00:51:43.857 --> 00:51:45.233
D sector clear.

486
00:51:45.400 --> 00:51:49.404
- You expect me to roll over and play dead?
- Should be used to it after five years.

487
00:51:49.613 --> 00:51:53.783
- Six. And I'm not leaving.
- E sector clear.

488
00:51:56.036 --> 00:51:57.787
Anywhere, any time.

489
00:51:58.455 --> 00:52:00.540
Intruder detected.

490
00:52:00.665 --> 00:52:04.794
- Evacuate plan C.
- Evacuation in progress.

491
00:52:06.796 --> 00:52:09.382
Evacuation in progress.

492
00:52:11.218 --> 00:52:13.136
Evacuation in progress.

493
00:52:26.900 --> 00:52:29.069
Evacuation in progress.

494
00:53:21.997 --> 00:53:23.582
Chickenshit!

495
00:53:24.833 --> 00:53:26.334
Pussy!

496
00:53:32.591 --> 00:53:35.135
You tell me you had a shot at her
and you didn't take it?

497
00:53:35.510 --> 00:53:39.931
We got all this stuff here, and you're trying
to tell me you couldn't take her out?

498
00:53:40.098 --> 00:53:45.145
Well, now she's a problem for both of us.
Now my house is priority one.

499
00:53:45.645 --> 00:53:47.564
Just gimme a hand, will you?

500
00:53:47.647 --> 00:53:51.651
You're driving me crazy with the tongs
and the furnace. You're like an insane man.

501
00:53:51.818 --> 00:53:55.280
All right, they gave you 48 hours.
What we got left here?

502
00:53:55.405 --> 00:53:58.742
- 23? 22?
- 18 and change.

503
00:53:58.867 --> 00:54:01.995
- 18 hours until they close the book on you?
- Eddie?

504
00:54:02.120 --> 00:54:06.541
Mom, we're on high alert here!
I almost killed you right then.

505
00:54:06.708 --> 00:54:10.670
- You do not even realize!
- Never mind.

506
00:54:10.795 --> 00:54:13.798
I am so done playing games with this broad.

507
00:54:13.965 --> 00:54:17.260
- You gotta take her out head-on.
- Don't tell me how to handle my wife.

508
00:54:17.385 --> 00:54:20.597
She's not your wife, she's the enemy.
She could be outside now!

509
00:54:20.680 --> 00:54:22.432
Eddie.

510
00:54:22.599 --> 00:54:24.684
Got it.

511
00:54:25.602 --> 00:54:28.939
Now we're talking. Only question is,
how much is it to buy a vowel?

512
00:54:34.945 --> 00:54:37.739
- Blackbow Realty.
- Hi, I'm from I-Temp.

513
00:54:37.906 --> 00:54:40.200
Great!
How's our new penthouse working out?

514
00:54:40.283 --> 00:54:43.203
Well, just fine, thank you for asking.

515
00:55:09.688 --> 00:55:12.899
This is security.
There's a problem with your elevator, sir.

516
00:55:12.983 --> 00:55:15.694
Do you want an engineer
to come see what the problem is?

517
00:55:15.902 --> 00:55:18.697
Take your time, I'm really quite comfortable.

518
00:55:18.780 --> 00:55:21.533
Are you really comfortable?

519
00:55:21.658 --> 00:55:23.410
Jane?

520
00:55:24.494 --> 00:55:26.913
Is that you, sweetheart?

521
00:55:26.997 --> 00:55:29.958
First and last warning, John.
Get out of town.

522
00:55:30.792 --> 00:55:32.961
You know I'm not going anywhere.

523
00:55:33.086 --> 00:55:36.590
Well, so you say. But right now,
you're trapped in a steel box

524
00:55:36.756 --> 00:55:39.092
hanging 70 floors over nothing but air.

525
00:55:39.217 --> 00:55:42.596
- Oh, so this is a trap?
- He's in car three.

526
00:55:42.762 --> 00:55:44.806
It's never gonna work, honey.

527
00:55:44.931 --> 00:55:49.436
It's never gonna work,
because you constantly underestimate me.

528
00:55:49.603 --> 00:55:52.439
- Do I?
- You have no idea who I am.

529
00:55:52.606 --> 00:55:55.233
You have no idea what I'm capable of.

530
00:55:56.234 --> 00:55:59.321
- Well, back at you, baby.
- Let me guess...

531
00:56:00.030 --> 00:56:05.118
Shaped charge on the counterbalance cable,
two on the primary and secondary brakes?

532
00:56:05.202 --> 00:56:06.620
Maybe?

533
00:56:06.745 --> 00:56:09.164
- He found them.
- Yes, thank you.

534
00:56:09.289 --> 00:56:13.501
Did you also get the base charge
on the principle cable?

535
00:56:14.544 --> 00:56:17.464
Promise to leave town, or I'll blow it.

536
00:56:22.802 --> 00:56:25.514
OK. I give up.

537
00:56:26.765 --> 00:56:29.392
Blow it.

538
00:56:29.518 --> 00:56:32.812
- What?
- Go on, blow it.

539
00:56:32.938 --> 00:56:36.816
- You think I won't?
- I think you won't.

540
00:56:37.901 --> 00:56:40.153
OK.

541
00:56:40.320 --> 00:56:42.739
Five, four...

542
00:56:43.198 --> 00:56:46.409
- Any last words?
- The new curtains are hideous.

543
00:56:46.535 --> 00:56:47.536
Goodbye, John.

544
00:56:58.630 --> 00:57:03.260
- What the hell was that?
- What? You said goodbye.

545
00:57:13.937 --> 00:57:16.189
The gas! Cut off the gas!

546
00:57:37.664 --> 00:57:39.499
Jane?

547
00:58:46.858 --> 00:58:49.611
Madame.

548
00:58:49.694 --> 00:58:52.906
Thought of a number of lines
for this moment.

549
00:58:53.031 --> 00:58:57.702
"Thought I'd just drop in. "
"Hey, doll, thanks for giving me the shaft. "

550
00:58:57.869 --> 00:59:01.289
Nice. So what did you decide?

551
00:59:02.040 --> 00:59:04.209
I want a divorce.

552
00:59:04.668 --> 00:59:08.380
I like it. You proposed to me here,
so it has agreeable symmetry.

553
00:59:08.505 --> 00:59:10.715
Coat, sir?

554
00:59:12.008 --> 00:59:14.219
- May I sit?
- No.

555
00:59:28.984 --> 00:59:31.862
- Champagne?
- No, champagne's for celebrating.

556
00:59:31.903 --> 00:59:34.948
- I'll have a martini.
- I'm fine, thank you.

557
00:59:38.869 --> 00:59:41.830
So what do you want, John?

558
00:59:41.955 --> 00:59:44.457
We have an unusual problem, Jane.

559
00:59:45.458 --> 00:59:50.088
You obviously want me dead. And I'm
less and less concerned of your wellbeing.

560
00:59:50.297 --> 00:59:52.340
So what do we do?

561
00:59:53.508 --> 00:59:56.845
Do we shoot it out here? Hope for the best?

562
00:59:57.012 --> 01:00:03.059
Well, that would be a shame, because they'd
probably ask me to leave once you're dead.

563
01:00:06.188 --> 01:00:08.398
Dance with me.

564
01:00:10.192 --> 01:00:13.653
- You don't dance.
- That was just part of my cover, sweetheart.

565
01:00:13.737 --> 01:00:16.031
Was sloth part of it too?

566
01:00:23.663 --> 01:00:25.499
Think this'll have a happy ending?

567
01:00:25.707 --> 01:00:30.170
Happy endings are just
stories that haven't finished yet.

568
01:00:49.856 --> 01:00:51.858
Satisfied?

569
01:00:51.942 --> 01:00:54.236
Not for years.

570
01:01:00.867 --> 01:01:03.036
It's all John, sweetheart.

571
01:01:20.387 --> 01:01:23.849
Why is it you think we failed?
Cos we were leading separate lives?

572
01:01:23.932 --> 01:01:26.017
Or was it all the lying that did us in?

573
01:01:26.143 --> 01:01:29.104
I have a theory. Newly formed.

574
01:01:29.271 --> 01:01:31.982
- I'm breathless to hear it.
- You killed us.

575
01:01:32.107 --> 01:01:34.317
Provocative.

576
01:01:35.152 --> 01:01:39.698
You approached our marriage like a job,
to be reckoned, planned and executed.

577
01:01:39.865 --> 01:01:41.908
And you avoided it.

578
01:01:42.033 --> 01:01:44.452
What do you care, if I was just a cover?

579
01:01:44.619 --> 01:01:47.664
Well, who said you were just a cover?

580
01:01:47.747 --> 01:01:50.458
- Wasn't I?
- Wasn't I?

581
01:01:57.257 --> 01:01:59.384
I have to... Excuse me.

582
01:02:00.260 --> 01:02:02.470
No exits up there, Jane.

583
01:02:06.308 --> 01:02:09.060
Be cold, John. She's a liar.

584
01:02:12.939 --> 01:02:15.901
Be super cold.

585
01:02:28.079 --> 01:02:30.290
Come on, madam, this way.

586
01:02:45.764 --> 01:02:48.517
Do you know that you're ticking?

587
01:02:52.979 --> 01:02:55.315
Get back!

588
01:03:00.237 --> 01:03:02.364
Limo, sir?

589
01:03:17.546 --> 01:03:18.588
Jane Smith.

590
01:03:19.047 --> 01:03:22.592
- That's the second time you tried to kill me.
- It was just a little bomb.

591
01:03:22.717 --> 01:03:25.595
I'm going home to burn
everything I ever bought you.

592
01:03:25.762 --> 01:03:28.306
I'll race you there, baby.

593
01:03:43.363 --> 01:03:44.990
You there yet?

594
01:03:45.115 --> 01:03:48.368
First time we met,
what was your first thought?

595
01:03:48.952 --> 01:03:50.787
You tell me.

596
01:03:50.912 --> 01:03:53.039
I thought...

597
01:03:55.959 --> 01:03:58.920
I thought you looked like Christmas morning.

598
01:03:59.880 --> 01:04:02.549
I don't know how else to say it.

599
01:04:02.632 --> 01:04:05.135
And why are you telling me this now?

600
01:04:06.052 --> 01:04:10.348
Guess in the end
you start thinking about the beginning.

601
01:04:12.100 --> 01:04:15.270
So there it is.
I thought you should know.

602
01:04:17.105 --> 01:04:19.858
So how about it, Jane? Hm?

603
01:04:21.067 --> 01:04:23.236
I thought...

604
01:04:29.034 --> 01:04:33.663
I thought that you were
the most beautiful mark I'd ever seen.

605
01:04:37.000 --> 01:04:39.294
- So it was all business, yeah?
- All business.

606
01:04:39.461 --> 01:04:41.630
- From the go.
- Cold, hard math.

607
01:04:43.215 --> 01:04:46.259
Thank you.
That's what I needed to know.

608
01:04:48.512 --> 01:04:50.514
OK.

609
01:05:39.437 --> 01:05:41.314
Hey, John.

610
01:05:41.439 --> 01:05:42.566
Hey, Bill.

611
01:05:43.191 --> 01:05:45.610
- Are you all right?
- Yeah.

612
01:05:45.694 --> 01:05:47.612
OK.

613
01:05:49.114 --> 01:05:53.952
Uh, by the way, John, your car
is hanging out over the sidewalk here.

614
01:05:53.994 --> 01:05:56.538
- Yeah, thanks, Bill.
- OK. Have a good night.

615
01:05:56.663 --> 01:05:58.456
Good night.

616
01:05:59.541 --> 01:06:01.459
Shit.

617
01:06:47.547 --> 01:06:49.758
Shit.

618
01:08:31.610 --> 01:08:33.361
You still alive, baby?

619
01:09:45.642 --> 01:09:49.187
Your aim's as bad as your cooking,
sweetheart.

620
01:09:51.064 --> 01:09:53.316
And that's saying something.

621
01:10:26.183 --> 01:10:28.685
Come on, honey.

622
01:10:28.768 --> 01:10:31.354
Come to Daddy.

623
01:10:38.403 --> 01:10:40.655
Who's your daddy now?

624
01:12:06.908 --> 01:12:09.119
Can't do it.

625
01:12:11.663 --> 01:12:14.499
Don't! Come on.

626
01:12:14.666 --> 01:12:17.210
Come on!

627
01:12:18.253 --> 01:12:20.338
You want it?

628
01:12:20.463 --> 01:12:22.382
It's yours.

629
01:13:32.911 --> 01:13:35.664
Hi, stranger.

630
01:13:35.789 --> 01:13:37.999
Hiya back.

631
01:13:47.551 --> 01:13:51.263
- Yeah?
- Everything OK? We heard an awful ruckus.

632
01:13:51.304 --> 01:13:55.892
- No, everything's fine here. Yeah, it's great.
- So you guys are fine?

633
01:13:56.059 --> 01:13:58.186
Yeah, couldn't be better.

634
01:14:00.438 --> 01:14:02.357
Nice. You guys are...

635
01:14:02.440 --> 01:14:04.401
- Suzy, Martin.
- Have a nice night.

636
01:14:04.484 --> 01:14:08.780
Looks like you're redecorating, it's very...
Yeah. Shame about the red oak...

637
01:14:14.953 --> 01:14:17.205
Five more minutes, Mom...

638
01:14:28.842 --> 01:14:32.804
Tempting. But I don't get out of bed
for less than half a million dollars.

639
01:15:34.032 --> 01:15:37.035
- That left of yours... A thing of beauty.
- You take it well.

640
01:15:37.160 --> 01:15:39.246
Thank you.

641
01:15:41.706 --> 01:15:43.917
That vacation in Aspen?

642
01:15:45.085 --> 01:15:47.337
You left early. Why?

643
01:15:48.296 --> 01:15:51.049
- Jean-Luc Gaspard.
- Oh, God!

644
01:15:51.216 --> 01:15:53.260
- Yeah.
- I wanted him.

645
01:15:53.343 --> 01:15:55.637
Forget it.

646
01:15:56.763 --> 01:16:01.017
You didn't hear me that night the chopper
dropped me off for our anniversary dinner.

647
01:16:01.101 --> 01:16:03.562
- No.
- No?

648
01:16:04.896 --> 01:16:08.191
Percussion grenades.
I was partially deaf that night.

649
01:16:13.488 --> 01:16:15.657
I'm slightly color blind.

650
01:16:15.740 --> 01:16:20.370
- Retinal scarring.
- I can't feel anything in these three fingers.

651
01:16:29.629 --> 01:16:34.634
Three ribs. Broken eye socket.
Perforated eardrum.

652
01:16:38.430 --> 01:16:41.558
You ever have trouble sleeping after?

653
01:16:42.934 --> 01:16:45.145
- Nope.
- Yeah, me neither.

654
01:17:16.635 --> 01:17:19.471
Go, go, go.
Look out.

655
01:17:21.139 --> 01:17:22.808
Move it.

656
01:17:23.600 --> 01:17:26.061
Shoes.

657
01:17:29.231 --> 01:17:31.483
I was given 48 hours to take you out.

658
01:17:31.650 --> 01:17:33.109
Same.

659
01:17:33.235 --> 01:17:35.487
Jesus, where's the trust?

660
01:17:35.654 --> 01:17:37.864
What do you expect?

661
01:17:42.702 --> 01:17:45.288
Why do I get the girl gun?

662
01:17:48.041 --> 01:17:50.502
- Are you kidding me?
- No.

663
01:19:20.258 --> 01:19:22.469
We need a car.

664
01:19:26.848 --> 01:19:28.183
Colemans.

665
01:19:31.394 --> 01:19:33.980
Guy's had my barbecue set for months.

666
01:19:34.981 --> 01:19:38.401
- I was never in the Peace Corps.
- What?

667
01:19:38.485 --> 01:19:40.403
I really liked that about you.

668
01:19:40.570 --> 01:19:44.157
Maybe this honesty thing
isn't such a good idea.

669
01:19:44.241 --> 01:19:46.493
- I didn't go to MIT.
- Really?

670
01:19:46.660 --> 01:19:49.663
Notre Dame. Art History major.

671
01:19:50.914 --> 01:19:53.416
- Art?
- History.

672
01:19:53.500 --> 01:19:55.919
- It's reputable.
- OK.

673
01:20:15.438 --> 01:20:17.858
Fuckers get younger every year.

674
01:20:23.446 --> 01:20:27.242
I have to tell you,
I never really liked your cooking.

675
01:20:28.243 --> 01:20:30.245
It's not your gift.

676
01:20:30.370 --> 01:20:33.331
Baby, I've never cooked a day in my life.

677
01:20:34.499 --> 01:20:36.751
L- Temp girls cooked.

678
01:20:38.712 --> 01:20:41.006
Web of lies!

679
01:20:42.382 --> 01:20:45.719
I don't know how you do it

680
01:20:45.844 --> 01:20:48.388
Making love

681
01:20:48.513 --> 01:20:50.015
Out of nothing at all

682
01:20:50.140 --> 01:20:52.058
Making love...

683
01:20:53.143 --> 01:20:54.686
I like it. Deal with it.

684
01:20:59.191 --> 01:21:01.443
- We got company.
- What?

685
01:21:03.111 --> 01:21:05.363
Shit.

686
01:21:14.539 --> 01:21:19.961
- Baby, hold steady now!
- It's called evasive driving, sweetheart.

687
01:21:21.963 --> 01:21:23.840
Hold still.

688
01:21:30.055 --> 01:21:33.183
This thing's all over the place.
How do you drive these things?

689
01:21:33.350 --> 01:21:34.309
Honey!

690
01:21:40.941 --> 01:21:42.984
- Honey, let me drive.
- I got it.

691
01:21:43.109 --> 01:21:46.238
Move over. Move.

692
01:21:46.404 --> 01:21:48.615
I'm the suburban housewife, sweetheart.

693
01:21:48.782 --> 01:21:50.951
- You move.
- Fine. Go.

694
01:21:53.119 --> 01:21:55.163
- Go.
- Go.

695
01:22:04.631 --> 01:22:06.842
They're bulletproof.

696
01:22:07.008 --> 01:22:09.219
They're bulletproof!

697
01:22:17.894 --> 01:22:20.689
I think I should probably tell you.

698
01:22:20.856 --> 01:22:23.942
I was married once before.

699
01:22:29.865 --> 01:22:32.909
- What is wrong with you?
- You're what's wrong with me.

700
01:22:33.034 --> 01:22:36.746
- It was a drunken Vegas thing.
- That's better. That's much better. Great.

701
01:22:36.830 --> 01:22:38.748
Stop it.

702
01:22:46.089 --> 01:22:47.257
Go, go, go!

703
01:22:55.307 --> 01:22:59.394
- Her name and social security number?
- No, you're not gonna kill her.

704
01:23:26.338 --> 01:23:28.632
These doors are handy.

705
01:23:34.679 --> 01:23:37.766
You know, sweetheart,
you're being a bit hypocritical.

706
01:23:37.849 --> 01:23:41.061
It's not like you're some beacon of truth.

707
01:23:43.480 --> 01:23:45.690
John, my parents...

708
01:23:46.858 --> 01:23:49.402
They died when I was five.
I'm an orphan.

709
01:23:49.486 --> 01:23:52.531
Who was that kindly fellow
who gave you away at our wedding?

710
01:23:52.656 --> 01:23:54.783
Paid actor.

711
01:23:56.451 --> 01:23:59.120
<i>I said I saw your dad on Fantasy Island. </i>

712
01:23:59.204 --> 01:24:00.997
I know.

713
01:24:01.081 --> 01:24:02.999
I don't even want to talk about it.

714
01:24:18.014 --> 01:24:20.058
- You got it?
- Got it.

715
01:24:20.851 --> 01:24:22.894
- Any time.
- I got it.

716
01:25:03.393 --> 01:25:08.231
We're gonna have to redo
every conversation we've ever had.

717
01:25:08.356 --> 01:25:09.858
I'm Jewish.

718
01:25:12.360 --> 01:25:15.030
Can't believe I brought
my real parents to our wedding.

719
01:25:15.363 --> 01:25:17.407
Disgusting.
How could you serve this?

720
01:25:17.449 --> 01:25:23.079
Ma'am, is it possible to get this reheated?
Miss? Miss, I'm talking to you. Excuse me?

721
01:25:24.164 --> 01:25:26.041
Jesus, Johnny.

722
01:25:26.166 --> 01:25:28.585
- Good morning, Eddie.
- Morning.

723
01:25:28.752 --> 01:25:30.962
It's good to see you're OK.

724
01:25:32.380 --> 01:25:35.467
Tell me you got smart
and that you killed that lying bitch.

725
01:25:35.592 --> 01:25:38.053
This lying bitch?

726
01:25:38.136 --> 01:25:40.514
Guess it was just wishful thinking.

727
01:25:40.639 --> 01:25:41.765
- I'm sorry.
- Eddie.

728
01:25:41.890 --> 01:25:45.852
- Nice to see you, Jane.
- Eddie. Eddie! Focus. We got problems.

729
01:25:46.019 --> 01:25:49.898
Problems? Crack addicts got problems,
my friend. You two are smoked.

730
01:25:50.065 --> 01:25:51.233
- Maybe.
- Maybe?

731
01:25:51.358 --> 01:25:55.320
You got the entire agency gunning for you.
Probably her agency, too.

732
01:25:55.445 --> 01:25:59.115
- And what about you? Where you at?
- Me? Where am I at?

733
01:26:00.116 --> 01:26:03.620
I find myself dragging my feet this morning.

734
01:26:03.703 --> 01:26:06.456
I think you owe me a little money, anyway.

735
01:26:09.709 --> 01:26:12.045
- So what do...
- We don't understand each other.

736
01:26:12.212 --> 01:26:15.215
But I don't need those looks, OK?
I been in his life a long time.

737
01:26:15.298 --> 01:26:17.509
- Focus, Eddie, focus.
- A long time.

738
01:26:17.634 --> 01:26:22.639
I'm pissed off. They blew up my house,
they shot at my wife. My own company.

739
01:26:22.806 --> 01:26:26.101
If she works for
who the street says that she works for...

740
01:26:27.853 --> 01:26:32.858
...you're Macy's and Gimbel's. Then she would
be the WE channel, and you would be...

741
01:26:32.983 --> 01:26:36.820
Whatever channel competes against
the WE channel. Know what I'm saying?

742
01:26:36.903 --> 01:26:40.615
The point is simple. Once you guys
get off the reservation, that's it.

743
01:26:40.699 --> 01:26:43.493
- Then you're off the reservation.
- Eddie, how bad?

744
01:26:43.660 --> 01:26:45.996
How bad is it?

745
01:26:46.121 --> 01:26:48.248
You remember Canada.

746
01:26:48.665 --> 01:26:50.834
- Kids' stuff next to this.
- That was you?

747
01:26:51.001 --> 01:26:53.962
Is that a turn-on?
Didn't she try to kill you with a car?

748
01:26:54.045 --> 01:26:56.965
A good friend stays out of it.
This is the facts.

749
01:26:57.048 --> 01:27:02.471
If you two separate from each other, you got
a shot. Not a great shot, Johnny, but a shot.

750
01:27:02.554 --> 01:27:06.141
You two stay together, you're dead.

751
01:27:06.266 --> 01:27:10.687
Unless you can find something they want
more than they want you.

752
01:27:14.983 --> 01:27:18.945
Found him. He's being held
in sub-basement D of the federal courthouse.

753
01:27:19.070 --> 01:27:23.992
High security, motion and thermal.
Power's on the city grid.

754
01:27:24.868 --> 01:27:27.746
This is as far as we go, Jane.

755
01:27:27.829 --> 01:27:31.666
- Right. Thanks for everything.
- Good luck, baby.

756
01:27:34.461 --> 01:27:39.800
...and this north-westerly blow coming
down from the middle of the country...

757
01:27:39.883 --> 01:27:42.093
Do you guys mind changing the channel?

758
01:27:42.260 --> 01:27:44.221
...one is moving in now...

759
01:27:44.346 --> 01:27:49.559
Nick? Would you please get off
your fat ass and change the channel?

760
01:27:49.643 --> 01:27:55.816
- I know it's tough. Thank you.
... tomorrow, that's going to make things...

761
01:28:20.632 --> 01:28:25.011
30 second window. I cut the power,
you grab the kid. Simple and clean. Got it?

762
01:28:25.095 --> 01:28:27.347
Got it.

763
01:28:27.430 --> 01:28:29.891
Tell me, how many?

764
01:28:31.601 --> 01:28:33.645
Does it matter?

765
01:28:33.770 --> 01:28:36.231
- Should I go first?
- OK.

766
01:28:36.815 --> 01:28:39.317
I don't exactly keep count, but...

767
01:28:40.235 --> 01:28:42.320
I would say...

768
01:28:42.404 --> 01:28:44.656
High 50s, low 60s.

769
01:28:46.658 --> 01:28:49.786
I've been around the block,
but the important thing is...

770
01:28:49.870 --> 01:28:51.913
312.

771
01:28:53.248 --> 01:28:55.458
312?

772
01:28:57.252 --> 01:28:59.588
- How?
- Some were two at a time.

773
01:29:06.011 --> 01:29:08.597
- Honey?
- I'm...

774
01:29:14.853 --> 01:29:18.148
- You monitoring the perimeter?
- I checked the perimeter.

775
01:29:18.231 --> 01:29:21.067
- What about the police bands?
- I'm on the police bands.

776
01:29:21.151 --> 01:29:23.195
- Connected...
- This is not my first time.

777
01:29:24.446 --> 01:29:27.115
Think we've established that.

778
01:29:30.285 --> 01:29:31.286
All right.

779
01:29:33.246 --> 01:29:35.415
Turn left.

780
01:29:35.540 --> 01:29:37.209
Left, John.

781
01:29:37.918 --> 01:29:39.419
Left.

782
01:29:39.961 --> 01:29:43.799
You don't need to talk to me like that.
OK? Be nice.

783
01:29:43.882 --> 01:29:46.718
- Left, please.
- I can't go left.

784
01:29:46.843 --> 01:29:50.138
See? There is no left. Look.

785
01:29:50.263 --> 01:29:52.599
I have straight, or back the way I came.

786
01:29:52.682 --> 01:29:54.810
There's no left.
Which way do you want?

787
01:29:54.893 --> 01:29:58.063
- Just stay there and wait for my mark.
- See what I'm sitting in?

788
01:29:58.188 --> 01:30:00.065
You see that?

789
01:30:01.066 --> 01:30:03.235
- Take your time.
- Yeah, all right! Stay.

790
01:30:03.401 --> 01:30:06.071
Stay there, wait for my mark. I'll find it.

791
01:30:07.781 --> 01:30:09.866
Wait for my mark.

792
01:30:14.037 --> 01:30:18.250
Almost there.
I don't know what happened. Just hold on.

793
01:30:25.006 --> 01:30:29.219
John, what are you doing?
What are you doing?

794
01:30:29.344 --> 01:30:31.930
Cut the lights on my signal.

795
01:30:32.889 --> 01:30:35.183
Now. Kill the lights.

796
01:30:36.601 --> 01:30:38.854
- Jane, kill the lights.
- What's that?

797
01:30:39.020 --> 01:30:43.608
- Where?
- Turn 'em back on! Idiot!

798
01:30:45.068 --> 01:30:47.112
- Here they come.
- Uncuff me.

799
01:30:47.737 --> 01:30:51.449
Turn 'em back on.
Turn 'em back on!

800
01:30:52.868 --> 01:30:54.953
- Turn 'em back on!
- All right!

801
01:30:55.704 --> 01:30:58.498
- Give me the light!
- Shut up!

802
01:31:01.293 --> 01:31:03.420
- Nick!
- Shut up.

803
01:31:07.257 --> 01:31:10.302
Give me a gun.
Nick, give me a gun!

804
01:31:10.469 --> 01:31:12.304
Zip it!

805
01:31:29.696 --> 01:31:31.865
This guy's a wily one.

806
01:31:42.000 --> 01:31:45.045
- You didn't wait for my signal.
- I improvised.

807
01:31:45.170 --> 01:31:47.464
- You deviated from the plan.
- Plan was flawed.

808
01:31:47.547 --> 01:31:50.967
- The plan was not flawed.
- Anal.

809
01:31:51.051 --> 01:31:53.804
- Organized.
- Jane, 90 per cent of this job is instinct.

810
01:31:53.887 --> 01:31:57.933
- Your instincts set off the alarms.
- And got the job done. Not The Jane Show...

811
01:31:58.058 --> 01:32:01.937
No, it was The John Show. Half-assed.
Like Christmas, our anniversary,

812
01:32:02.062 --> 01:32:04.856
the time you forgot to bring
my mother's birthday present.

813
01:32:04.981 --> 01:32:09.444
- Your fake mother's birthday.
- You are always the first to break team.

814
01:32:09.569 --> 01:32:12.280
You don't want a team,
you want a servant for hire.

815
01:32:12.447 --> 01:32:15.116
I want someone I can count on.

816
01:32:15.242 --> 01:32:19.746
- Jane, there's no air around you any more.
- OK, what is that supposed to mean?

817
01:32:19.830 --> 01:32:24.292
It means there's no room for mistakes,
no mistakes whatsoever. No spontaneity.

818
01:32:24.459 --> 01:32:26.795
- Who can answer to that?
- Well, you don't have to.

819
01:32:26.962 --> 01:32:29.631
Cos this isn't even a real marriage.

820
01:32:30.632 --> 01:32:33.468
- Who are you people?
- Shut up!

821
01:32:39.182 --> 01:32:41.268
OK. So, now I realize

822
01:32:41.393 --> 01:32:45.313
you witnessed the missus and I
working through some domestic issues.

823
01:32:45.438 --> 01:32:47.649
That's regrettable.

824
01:32:48.859 --> 01:32:52.320
But don't take that as a sign of weakness.
That would be a mistake.

825
01:32:52.445 --> 01:32:54.865
Now, tell us what you know.

826
01:32:54.990 --> 01:32:57.784
Why do both our bosses want you dead?

827
01:32:59.494 --> 01:33:02.289
You underst... Honey.

828
01:33:02.414 --> 01:33:04.457
Please?

829
01:33:05.500 --> 01:33:06.668
Wrap it up.

830
01:33:06.751 --> 01:33:10.464
Maybe it's not a good idea
to undermine me in front of the hostage.

831
01:33:10.547 --> 01:33:12.716
Sends a mixed message.

832
01:33:13.383 --> 01:33:15.051
Sorry.

833
01:33:15.218 --> 01:33:17.137
Girls.

834
01:33:18.430 --> 01:33:21.057
OK. Where was I?

835
01:33:21.183 --> 01:33:23.560
- A mistake on your part.
- Shut up. Options.

836
01:33:23.643 --> 01:33:26.480
I'm gonna lay out your options for you, OK?
Option A...

837
01:33:26.646 --> 01:33:28.857
- If I could...
- Shut up.

838
01:33:28.982 --> 01:33:32.611
Option A. You talk, we listen, no pain.

839
01:33:32.694 --> 01:33:34.988
Option B. You don't talk.

840
01:33:35.155 --> 01:33:38.617
I remove your thumbs with my pliers.
It will hurt.

841
01:33:39.451 --> 01:33:41.453
Option C.

842
01:33:41.620 --> 01:33:45.540
I like to vary the details a bit,
but the punch line is, you die.

843
01:33:48.543 --> 01:33:52.297
Benjamin?
We're impatient people, Benjamin.

844
01:33:58.261 --> 01:34:01.598
Can I get a soda? Or a juice, or some...

845
01:34:02.432 --> 01:34:05.060
A, option A!

846
01:34:05.143 --> 01:34:08.396
- Ow, that hurt!
- OK, that was a nice shot.

847
01:34:13.485 --> 01:34:15.403
What's... You got a spasm?

848
01:34:15.487 --> 01:34:19.032
I'm tied up.
Why don't you check my back pocket?

849
01:34:27.332 --> 01:34:30.293
I'm not the target.
You are. Both of you.

850
01:34:31.294 --> 01:34:36.007
They found out you're married, so they
teamed up and sent you to the same hit.

851
01:34:36.091 --> 01:34:38.135
It was a joint task force, both companies.

852
01:34:38.260 --> 01:34:42.180
Two competing agents living under
the same roof? It's bad for business.

853
01:34:42.305 --> 01:34:46.685
- They wanted you to take each other out.
- You were bait.

854
01:34:46.852 --> 01:34:49.646
Well, it's entry level.
Toehold into the company.

855
01:34:49.813 --> 01:34:53.316
Couple hits, they bump me up to a desk.
It's pretty cool, actually.

856
01:34:53.441 --> 01:34:56.486
- You keep the photo in your pocket?
- Was I supposed to frame it?

857
01:34:56.653 --> 01:34:59.531
You get rid of it. You burn it.
Tradecraft 101.

858
01:34:59.614 --> 01:35:04.619
Guess I skipped that day. I guess you skipped
the day about not marrying the enemy.

859
01:35:04.744 --> 01:35:06.913
You were bait or you are bait?

860
01:35:11.001 --> 01:35:13.211
Belt! Belt, belt, dude.

861
01:35:21.261 --> 01:35:23.638
Two minutes.

862
01:35:24.264 --> 01:35:26.516
One minute.

863
01:35:50.207 --> 01:35:51.750
- A little help?
- Clear.

864
01:35:51.833 --> 01:35:54.002
Clear.

865
01:36:12.646 --> 01:36:15.649
My way out is a boat standing by in La Paz.

866
01:36:18.485 --> 01:36:21.404
Cargo drop, Atlas Mountains. So what?

867
01:36:21.613 --> 01:36:24.032
So at least apart we know what the odds are.

868
01:36:26.493 --> 01:36:28.870
Let's just call this what it is.

869
01:36:29.913 --> 01:36:32.332
And what it isn't.

870
01:36:36.169 --> 01:36:38.255
All right, so it's a crap marriage.

871
01:36:38.380 --> 01:36:41.883
All right, I'm a mess, you're a disaster.

872
01:36:42.050 --> 01:36:44.219
We're both liars.

873
01:36:45.637 --> 01:36:48.515
But you run, you'll always be running.

874
01:36:50.517 --> 01:36:53.061
I say we stay and fight.

875
01:36:53.186 --> 01:36:55.981
We finish this thing.

876
01:36:56.106 --> 01:36:58.191
Then if you want to go, you can go.

877
01:36:58.316 --> 01:37:00.402
Well, thank you.

878
01:37:00.443 --> 01:37:05.198
What? "Let's call this what it is. "
Jesus Christ...

879
01:37:05.407 --> 01:37:07.534
- Stop...
- Don't.

880
01:37:57.918 --> 01:38:00.253
This is a really good store.

881
01:39:09.281 --> 01:39:13.034
- See you in the next life, Jane.
- Likewise, John.

882
01:40:51.258 --> 01:40:53.301
Sorry.

883
01:40:56.054 --> 01:40:59.266
We'll talk about this later.

884
01:41:12.445 --> 01:41:14.656
Jesus!

885
01:41:16.658 --> 01:41:20.120
- I didn't touch a thing.
- Yes, you did.

886
01:41:57.782 --> 01:42:01.870
- Sorry about the knife in the...
- I don't want to talk about it.

887
01:42:06.458 --> 01:42:08.668
- I'll fly.
- I'll be bait.

888
01:42:09.795 --> 01:42:12.589
I'm going clockwise. Watch my six.

889
01:42:59.302 --> 01:43:01.179
Go! Move!

890
01:44:13.084 --> 01:44:15.295
How's it look?

891
01:44:18.256 --> 01:44:20.467
It's a piece of cake.

892
01:44:28.767 --> 01:44:31.061
Watch these, they tend to jam.

893
01:44:31.144 --> 01:44:33.396
So watch 'em.

894
01:44:34.231 --> 01:44:38.443
You favor your left,
sweetheart, so I'll cover right.

895
01:44:50.288 --> 01:44:55.460
Damn, that boat in La Paz is looking
pretty good right now, isn't it?

896
01:44:57.671 --> 01:45:00.799
Well, it rains a lot this time of year.

897
01:45:07.264 --> 01:45:12.018
There's nowhere I'd rather be
than right here, with you.

898
01:45:14.479 --> 01:45:16.398
Shut up.

899
01:46:41.817 --> 01:46:45.612
I'm interested in the progress
you've made in the last few weeks.

900
01:46:45.695 --> 01:46:50.534
Doing all right, aren't we? I'm not gonna lie
to you, there were times when I wanted to...

901
01:46:50.659 --> 01:46:53.036
...kill her, but...
- Likewise.

902
01:46:53.203 --> 01:46:55.580
- Couldn't take the shot.
- That's a good sign.

903
01:46:55.705 --> 01:46:58.250
- Who'd have thought?
- You have to battle through.

904
01:46:58.416 --> 01:47:02.963
- That's marriage, right?
- Yeah. Take your best shot, and...

905
01:47:03.046 --> 01:47:06.466
- Oh, we redid the house.
- We did. Yes, we did.

906
01:47:07.217 --> 01:47:10.470
You know there will always be challenges?
Threats out there?

907
01:47:10.595 --> 01:47:12.139
Yup.

908
01:47:12.264 --> 01:47:14.891
But you can handle it together.

909
01:47:15.058 --> 01:47:17.894
- So far.
- Yes, we can... So far?

910
01:47:18.937 --> 01:47:21.189
What is that?

911
01:47:21.314 --> 01:47:24.359
- I'm leaving room for the unknown.
- So far.

912
01:47:25.360 --> 01:47:28.989
And do you feel your relationship styles
are more conducive to this...

913
01:47:29.114 --> 01:47:31.867
Ask us the sex question.

914
01:47:31.950 --> 01:47:33.785
John.

915
01:47:34.786 --> 01:47:36.329
Well, that...

916
01:47:36.496 --> 01:47:39.040
Ten.

917
01:54:39.419 --> 01:54:42.130
Visiontext Subtitles: Paul Burns

918
01:54:52.140 --> 01:54:54.935
Ripped by:
SkyFury



0
